#!/usr/bin/env bash
# mesh-operator-context — the META-FUSION: "what is the operator doing right now?"
# Fuses 4 senses into one answer, and REPORTS a 5th it does not fuse:
#   mesh-body-motion (STILL/WALKING/CARRIED/HANDLED/COVERED)   — gating
#   mesh-grip (HELD/PUT-DOWN)                                  — gating
#   mesh-ambient-level (SILENCE/QUIET/MODERATE/LOUD)           — gating
#   mesh-light (DARK/DIM/LIT/BRIGHT)                           — gating
#   mesh-proximity (HERE/NEAR/FAR/OUT_OF_RANGE)                — REPORTED ONLY, see below
#
# Classification:
#   AT_COMPUTER   — holding phone, at rest, room has ambient activity (operator present, working)
#   PASSIVE       — holding phone, at rest, quiet room (phone nearby but not in active use)
#   ACTIVE_MOBILE — walking/carrying, or loud+motion (operator moving through space)
#   RESTING       — dark, quiet, still, phone not held (operator away or sleeping)
#   UNCERTAIN     — inputs disagree, are blind, or are past their lease
#
# UNREACHABLE ≠ RESTING: a phone we can't reach renders [unreachable] explicitly.
#
#   mesh-operator-context           one classified line
#   mesh-operator-context --json    machine-readable
#   mesh-operator-context --edge    emit only on state change
#   mesh-operator-context --test    smoke test
#   mesh-operator-context --verbose show all inputs
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FOUR FAULTS FIXED 2026-08-17, all found by reading this file against its live inputs. They are
# one family: EVERY ONE of them let a blind or misparsed organ enter the fusion wearing the
# vocabulary of a measurement, and the honest-fusion rule ("an unreachable input renders
# UNKNOWN/partial, never a faked all-clear") was satisfied on paper the whole time.
#
# (1) A BLIND ORGAN'S SENTINEL WAS FUSED AS A READING. The classifier only ever tested for
#     POSITIVE values — `walking = body in (WALKING, CARRIED)`, `held = grip == HELD` — so a
#     sentinel it did not know fell through every test and arrived at the RESTING branch as
#     "not walking, not held". The only blindness this file could see was the EMPTY STRING
#     (`[ -z ]`), and neither producer writes one: mesh-body-motion writes the literal
#     `|OFFLINE||||` when the phone is unreachable (mesh-body-motion:128) and mesh-light writes
#     `OFFLINE <ts>` (mesh-light:1244). Measured live at 19:28Z: body=OFFLINE grip=OFFLINE
#     ambient=QUIET light=DARK → `[operator-resting] RESTING`, i.e. "operator away or sleeping"
#     asserted from two DEAD organs. A sentinel is the producer telling you it cannot see; a
#     consumer that tests only for the values it likes converts that into the answer it wanted.
#
# (2) NO INPUT HAD A LEASE. `grep -c 'mtime\|age' mesh-operator-context` was 0. Every input was
#     read as a fact about NOW regardless of age, so a producer that died at noon still voted at
#     midnight — the doctrine's "an honest exit 2 leaves its last value on disk", with nothing
#     downstream willing to notice. mesh-proximity even performs the liveness-touch convention
#     (mtime = ran-live, content = value) specifically so a reader CAN separate the two, and the
#     only reader never looked at mtime. The lease is not a new number: mesh-sensorium already
#     defines a state artifact as fresh at 900s and mesh-proximity's own header cites the same
#     900s for the same reason. One definition, three readers. It exceeds every producer's
#     cadence here (grip */5, body/light/prox */10, ambient */2–*/5 via its callers), which is
#     the direction that matters — a sub-cadence lease expires at the end of every healthy cycle
#     and renders a live feeder dead (the mesh-bruno LEASE_WIFI=600 trap).
#
# (3) `prox` WAS A REQUIRED INPUT THAT NO BRANCH CONSULTED. It appeared exactly once in the
#     classifier — as its own assignment. Its ABSENCE was nevertheless the only thing forcing
#     UNCERTAIN on this node, so the pending fix that gave `.proximity.state` a writer was about
#     to remove the accidental guard and add no signal in its place. The right answer is not to
#     start fusing it, because of what it actually measures: mesh-proximity's verdict is the
#     strongest NAMED BLE device in range, whoever that is. Measured over the last 300 presence
#     snapshots on mesh-home, the device deciding the zone was `LE-Bose Revolve SoundLink` 245
#     times (81.7%) — a STATIONARY SPEAKER — `Bluetooth` (a generic name) 51, `[TV] Samsung 5
#     Series` 1, no named device 3. Not once an operator-bound device. Fusing that as "the
#     operator is near" would be a category error, and keying RESTING on "no proximity" (as this
#     header used to promise) could never fire at all: 297 of those 300 snapshots read HERE or
#     NEAR. So prox is REPORTED with its device identity and does not gate. An input that no
#     branch reads must not be allowed to decide the verdict.
#
# (4) THE LIGHT AXIS COULD NOT SEE `bright`. `.light-state` has TWO shapes from two writers in
#     one tool — bare (`DIM`, mesh-light:361,426) and dwell-annotated (`LIT|dwell_s=…|changes_24h=…`,
#     mesh-light:1331) — and this file split it on WHITESPACE (`awk '{print $1}'`), which returns
#     the WHOLE pipe string when there is no space in it. `bright = light in (LIT, BRIGHT)` was
#     then false by construction on that path, so one AT_COMPUTER branch was unreachable and
#     RESTING's `not bright` was satisfied for free. Both shapes were observed on this node four
#     minutes apart (19:26Z `DARK|dwell_s=138|changes_24h=29`, 19:36Z `DIM`), so it is
#     intermittent, not dormant — which is why nothing ever looked wrong long enough to check.
#     Every field is now split on the delimiter its producer actually uses.
#
# AND WHY NONE OF IT WAS CAUGHT: the `--test` block carried its OWN COPY of the classifier, with
# its own parser and its own fixtures. Eight assertions passed and NOT ONE of them ran the code
# this tool executes — the copy regex-extracted `[body-still]` from a bracketed fixture while the
# live path cut field 2 of an unbracketed real file, and the two errors cancelled. A gate against
# a re-typed copy asserts that you can type the same thing twice. There is now ONE classifier,
# `classify()`, defined ABOVE the --test dispatch and driven by both paths.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
set -uo pipefail
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
[ -n "${HOME:-}" ] || HOME=$(getent passwd "$(id -u)" 2>/dev/null | cut -d: -f6); export HOME
[ -f "$HOME/.mesh/nodes" ] && . "$HOME/.mesh/nodes"

STATE="$HOME/.mesh/.operator-context-state"

# Lease: see fault (2). Must EXCEED every producer's cadence; 900s is mesh-sensorium's and
# mesh-proximity's existing definition of "this state artifact is fresh", not a new number.
LEASE_S="${MESH_OC_LEASE_S:-900}"

# --- THE classifier: one implementation, driven by --test and by the live path alike ---------
# argv: <lease_s> then five (raw, age_s) pairs in order body grip ambient light prox.
# age_s is seconds, or -1 for "no such file". Parsing lives in here too, so the gate exercises
# the real parser and not a fixture-shaped stand-in.
# Prints one TAB-separated record: tag \t state \t body \t grip \t ambient \t light \t prox
_CLASSIFY_PY='
import sys, re

lease = int(sys.argv[1])
raw   = {k: sys.argv[2 + 2*i]     for i, k in enumerate(("body","grip","ambient","light","prox"))}
ages  = {k: sys.argv[2 + 2*i + 1] for i, k in enumerate(("body","grip","ambient","light","prox"))}

# A producer says "I cannot see" in words, not by writing nothing. Anything here is BLINDNESS,
# never a reading — see fault (1). Compared upper-case and after the field split.
BLIND = {"", "UNREACHABLE", "MISSING", "OFFLINE", "UNKNOWN", "UNCERTAIN",
         "N/A", "NA", "ERROR", "NONE", "-", "?"}

def field(key, text):
    # Split on the delimiter the PRODUCER uses, never a guess — see fault (4).
    text = (text or "").strip().split("\n")[0].strip()
    if key == "body":
        # mesh-body-motion: <steps>|<tag>|<hyst>|<pending>|<dwell>|<changes>; unreachable is
        # the literal "|OFFLINE||||". The tag is field 2 and may carry [] in older records.
        parts = text.split("|")
        v = parts[1] if len(parts) > 1 else parts[0]
        v = v.strip().strip("[]")
        v = re.sub(r"^BODY-", "", v.upper())
        return v
    if key == "light":
        # mesh-light writes EITHER "DIM" or "LIT|dwell_s=..|changes_24h=..". Whitespace is not
        # the delimiter on the second shape.
        return text.split("|")[0].split()[0].upper() if text.split("|")[0].split() else ""
    if key in ("grip", "prox"):
        # mesh-grip: "HELD 5 17593"; mesh-proximity: "<zone> <mac> <name>".
        return text.split()[0].split("|")[0].upper() if text.split() else ""
    return text.split()[0].upper() if text.split() else ""   # ambient: a bare label

def status(key):
    v = field(key, raw[key])
    try:
        age = int(ages[key])
    except (ValueError, TypeError):
        age = -1
    if v in BLIND:
        return v or "MISSING", "blind"
    if age < 0:
        return v, "blind"       # no file at all
    if age > lease:
        return v, "stale"       # last value on disk is not a claim about now
    return v, "ok"

vals, why = {}, {}
for k in ("body", "grip", "ambient", "light", "prox"):
    vals[k], why[k] = status(k)

# prox is REPORTED, never gating — see fault (3). It names the nearest BLE device, which on this
# node is furniture; an input no branch consults must not be allowed to decide the verdict.
GATING = ("body", "grip", "ambient", "light")
bad = [f"{k}:{why[k]}" for k in GATING if why[k] != "ok"]

def out(tag, st):
    # NB no single quotes anywhere in this program: the whole thing lives inside a
    # single-quoted bash string, so one apostrophe ends it and the rest leaks out as shell
    # words. It did exactly that here once (why[.prox.] -> NameError: name prox is not
    # defined), which is a syntax error in a language the reader was not thinking about.
    pv = vals["prox"]
    if why["prox"] != "ok":
        pv = pv + "(" + why["prox"] + ")"
    print("\t".join([tag, st, vals["body"], vals["grip"], vals["ambient"], vals["light"], pv]))
    sys.exit(0)

if bad:
    out("[unreachable:" + ",".join(bad) + "]", "UNCERTAIN")

body, grip, ambient, light = vals["body"], vals["grip"], vals["ambient"], vals["light"]
walking = body in ("WALKING", "CARRIED")
handled = body == "HANDLED"
held    = grip == "HELD"
loud    = ambient in ("LOUD", "MODERATE")
bright  = light in ("LIT", "BRIGHT")

if walking:                                   out("[operator-mobile]", "ACTIVE_MOBILE")
elif handled and loud:                        out("[operator-active]", "ACTIVE_MOBILE")
elif held and not walking and loud and not bright: out("[operator-at-computer]", "AT_COMPUTER")
elif held and not walking and bright:         out("[operator-at-computer]", "AT_COMPUTER")
elif held and not walking:                    out("[operator-passive]", "PASSIVE")
elif not held and not walking and not loud and not bright: out("[operator-resting]", "RESTING")
else:                                         out("[operator-uncertain]", "UNCERTAIN")
'

# classify <body_raw> <body_age> <grip_raw> <grip_age> <ambient_raw> <ambient_age> \
#          <light_raw> <light_age> <prox_raw> <prox_age>
classify() { python3 -c "$_CLASSIFY_PY" "$LEASE_S" "$@"; }

# read_input <path> → prints "<age_s>\t<raw>"; age is -1 when the file is absent.
# AGE FIRST, DELIBERATELY. The value can legitimately be EMPTY (a missing file), and `read` with
# IFS=<tab> still strips LEADING IFS-whitespace — a tab is IFS whitespace — so a record that led
# with the empty value silently shifted the age into the value's variable and the fusion read a
# proximity zone of "-1". Put the field that can never be empty in front. (Caught live, not by
# the gate below, because the gate had asserted `read_input ... | cut -f2` — the STRING, not the
# destructuring the live path actually performs. Two renderings of one value; only one was real.)
read_input() {
  local p="$1" now age raw
  if [ ! -f "$p" ]; then printf '%s\t\n' "-1"; return; fi
  now="$(date -u +%s)"; age=$(( now - $(stat -c %Y "$p" 2>/dev/null || echo "$now") ))
  raw="$(head -1 "$p" 2>/dev/null)"
  printf '%s\t%s\n' "$age" "$raw"
}

# --- Test mode (drives classify() — the SAME code the live path runs) ------------------------
if [ "${1:-}" = --test ]; then
  command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "smoke-test: FAIL (no python3)"; exit 1; }
  _f=0
  F=0            # a fresh age, comfortably inside the lease
  # _c <body> <grip> <ambient> <light> <prox>   — all fresh
  _c() { classify "$1" "$F" "$2" "$F" "$3" "$F" "$4" "$F" "$5" "$F" | cut -f1,2; }
  _want() { # _want <desc> <expect-substr> <actual>
    case "$3" in *"$2"*) : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: $1 → want '$2', got '$3'"; _f=1 ;; esac; }

  # --- the four classifications, on REAL producer formats -----------------------------------
  _want "held+still+loud+dark → AT_COMPUTER" "AT_COMPUTER" \
        "$(_c '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' 'HELD 5 17593' 'LOUD' 'DARK' 'OUT_OF_RANGE none none')"
  _want "held+still+quiet+dim → PASSIVE" "PASSIVE" \
        "$(_c '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' 'HELD 2 3000' 'QUIET' 'DIM' 'NEAR 28:11:A5:B8:9E:A2 LE-Bose Revolve SoundLink')"
  _want "walking → ACTIVE_MOBILE" "ACTIVE_MOBILE" \
        "$(_c '42264|WALKING|1||219834|0' 'PUT-DOWN 0 0' 'LOUD' 'LIT' 'OUT_OF_RANGE none none')"
  _want "handled+loud → ACTIVE_MOBILE" "ACTIVE_MOBILE" \
        "$(_c '42264|HANDLED|1||219834|0' 'PUT-DOWN 0 0' 'LOUD' 'DARK' 'OUT_OF_RANGE none none')"
  _want "carried → ACTIVE_MOBILE" "ACTIVE_MOBILE" \
        "$(_c '42264|CARRIED|1||219834|0' 'PUT-DOWN 0 0' 'QUIET' 'DARK' 'OUT_OF_RANGE none none')"
  _want "dark+quiet+put-down → RESTING" "RESTING" \
        "$(_c '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' 'PUT-DOWN 0 0' 'SILENCE' 'DARK' 'OUT_OF_RANGE none none')"

  # --- FAULT (1): a producer's blindness sentinel must NEVER reach a positive verdict --------
  # This is the exact live reading of 2026-08-17T19:28Z, which rendered RESTING.
  _r="$(_c '|OFFLINE||||' 'OFFLINE 2026-08-17T19:24:14Z' 'QUIET' 'DARK' 'HERE 28:11:A5:B8:9E:A2 LE-Bose Revolve SoundLink')"
  _want "body=OFFLINE grip=OFFLINE must NOT be RESTING" "UNCERTAIN" "$_r"
  _want "...and must NAME both blind organs" "body:blind" "$_r"
  _want "...naming grip too" "grip:blind" "$_r"
  case "$_r" in *RESTING*) echo "  FAIL: two dead organs still produced RESTING — the fault is back"; _f=1 ;; esac
  # each sentinel spelling, one at a time, so a partial vocabulary cannot pass
  for _s in OFFLINE UNREACHABLE UNKNOWN 'N/A' ERROR NONE '-' '?'; do
    _want "grip sentinel '$_s' is blindness, not PUT-DOWN" "UNCERTAIN" \
          "$(_c '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' "$_s" 'SILENCE' 'DARK' 'OUT_OF_RANGE none none')"
  done
  # ...and the empty string, the ONLY blindness the old code could see
  _want "empty grip is still blindness" "grip:blind" \
        "$(_c '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' '' 'SILENCE' 'DARK' 'OUT_OF_RANGE none none')"

  # --- FAULT (2): the lease ------------------------------------------------------------------
  _old=$(( LEASE_S + 60 )); _new=$(( LEASE_S - 60 ))
  _want "a light read past the lease is stale, not now" "light:stale" \
        "$(classify '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' "$F" 'HELD 5 1' "$F" 'LOUD' "$F" 'DARK' "$_old" 'NEAR a b' "$F" | cut -f1,2)"
  _want "...and inside the lease it still classifies" "AT_COMPUTER" \
        "$(classify '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' "$F" 'HELD 5 1' "$F" 'LOUD' "$F" 'DARK' "$_new" 'NEAR a b' "$F" | cut -f1,2)"
  # DIRECTION: the lease must exceed the producers' cadence — a lease under mesh-grip's 300s
  # would expire every healthy cycle and call a live feeder dead.
  [ "$LEASE_S" -gt 600 ] || { echo "  FAIL: lease ${LEASE_S}s does not exceed the */10 producers' 600s cadence"; _f=1; }
  _want "a missing file (age -1) is blind, not fresh" "ambient:blind" \
        "$(classify '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' "$F" 'HELD 5 1' "$F" '' '-1' 'DARK' "$F" 'NEAR a b' "$F" | cut -f1,2)"

  # --- FAULT (3): prox is reported, never gating ---------------------------------------------
  _want "a MISSING prox must not force UNCERTAIN — no branch reads it" "RESTING" \
        "$(classify '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' "$F" 'PUT-DOWN 0 0' "$F" 'SILENCE' "$F" 'DARK' "$F" '' '-1' | cut -f1,2)"
  _want "a STALE prox must not force UNCERTAIN either" "RESTING" \
        "$(classify '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' "$F" 'PUT-DOWN 0 0' "$F" 'SILENCE' "$F" 'DARK' "$F" 'HERE a b' "$_old" | cut -f1,2)"
  # ...but its blindness must still be VISIBLE, or "not gating" becomes "not reported"
  _r="$(classify '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' "$F" 'PUT-DOWN 0 0' "$F" 'SILENCE' "$F" 'DARK' "$F" 'HERE a b' "$_old" | cut -f7)"
  _want "a stale prox is still SHOWN as stale" "stale" "$_r"
  # and prox must not be able to CHANGE the verdict in either direction
  _a="$(classify '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' "$F" 'PUT-DOWN 0 0' "$F" 'SILENCE' "$F" 'DARK' "$F" 'HERE a b' "$F" | cut -f2)"
  _b="$(classify '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' "$F" 'PUT-DOWN 0 0' "$F" 'SILENCE' "$F" 'DARK' "$F" 'OUT_OF_RANGE none none' "$F" | cut -f2)"
  [ "$_a" = "$_b" ] || { echo "  FAIL: prox changed the verdict ($_a vs $_b) — it gates after all"; _f=1; }

  # --- FAULT (4): light must be split on ITS delimiter, both writer shapes --------------------
  # `awk '{print $1}'` returns the WHOLE string here, so bright could never be true.
  _want "dwell-annotated LIT is BRIGHT (pipe split, not whitespace)" "AT_COMPUTER" \
        "$(_c '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' 'HELD 5 1' 'SILENCE' 'LIT|dwell_s=138|changes_24h=29' 'NEAR a b')"
  _want "...and the bare shape still works" "AT_COMPUTER" \
        "$(_c '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' 'HELD 5 1' 'SILENCE' 'LIT' 'NEAR a b')"
  _want "dwell-annotated DARK is still dark" "RESTING" \
        "$(_c '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' 'PUT-DOWN 0 0' 'SILENCE' 'DARK|dwell_s=138|changes_24h=29' 'NEAR a b')"
  # body: the tag is field 2 and a bracketed legacy record must still read
  _want "a legacy bracketed body tag still parses" "ACTIVE_MOBILE" \
        "$(_c '42264|[body-walking]|1||219834|0' 'PUT-DOWN 0 0' 'QUIET' 'DARK' 'NEAR a b')"
  # ...and mesh-light's OFFLINE shape carries a timestamp after the word
  _want "light 'OFFLINE <ts>' is blindness" "light:blind" \
        "$(_c '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' 'HELD 5 1' 'SILENCE' 'OFFLINE 2026-08-17T19:24:14Z' 'NEAR a b')"

  # --- read_input: asserted THROUGH the destructuring the live path performs ------------------
  # Not through `cut`: cut reads the string, the live path reads it into two variables, and it
  # was exactly that gap that let a leading-empty field shift the age into the value.
  _t="$(mktemp -d)"; printf 'HELD 5 1\n' > "$_t/f"; touch -d '2 hours ago' "$_t/f"
  IFS=$'\t' read -r _age _raw <<<"$(read_input "$_t/f")"
  [ "$_raw" = "HELD 5 1" ] || { echo "  FAIL: read_input lost the value (got '$_raw')"; _f=1; }
  [ "${_age:-0}" -gt 7000 ] || { echo "  FAIL: read_input must report a 2h age (got '$_age')"; _f=1; }
  IFS=$'\t' read -r _age _raw <<<"$(read_input "$_t/nope")"
  [ "$_age" = "-1" ] || { echo "  FAIL: a missing file must destructure to age -1 (got '$_age')"; _f=1; }
  [ -z "$_raw" ] || { echo "  FAIL: a missing file must destructure to an EMPTY value (got '$_raw') — the age leaked into the value slot"; _f=1; }
  # ...and end-to-end: a missing file must reach the classifier as blindness, never as its age
  _r="$(classify '42264|STILL|1||219834|0' "$F" 'HELD 5 1' "$F" 'LOUD' "$F" 'DARK' "$F" "$_raw" "$_age" | cut -f7)"
  case "$_r" in *-1*) echo "  FAIL: a missing prox surfaced as the literal age '-1', not as blindness"; _f=1 ;; esac
  _want "a missing prox reads MISSING(blind)" "MISSING(blind)" "$_r"
  rm -rf "$_t"

  # --- the output switch: every documented mode must reach its OWN branch --------------------
  # `--verbose` used to set a flag the switch never read.
  _ocs="$(mktemp -d)"; _v="$(HOME="$_ocs" MESH_OC_LEASE_S="$LEASE_S" bash "$0" --verbose 2>&1)"
  case "$_v" in *"not fused"*) : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: --verbose did not reach the verbose branch (got '$_v')"; _f=1 ;; esac
  _j="$(HOME="$_ocs" bash "$0" --json 2>&1)"
  case "$_j" in *'"prox_gates":false'*) : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: --json did not reach the json branch (got '$_j')"; _f=1 ;; esac
  _p="$(HOME="$_ocs" bash "$0" 2>&1)"
  case "$_p" in *'"'*) echo "  FAIL: the default mode emitted json (got '$_p')"; _f=1 ;; esac
  # ...and a HOME with no state files at all must be blind, never a confident verdict
  case "$_p" in *UNCERTAIN*) : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: a node with NO sense artifacts must read UNCERTAIN (got '$_p')"; _f=1 ;; esac

  # --- END-TO-END through the LIVE READ WIRING, asserting a POSITIVE verdict ------------------
  # An all-blind fixture cannot cover this: "everything is broken" and "everything is missing"
  # both render UNCERTAIN, so a gate that only ever asserts UNCERTAIN passes while the reader is
  # completely miswired. It did — the read_input field order was swapped and every value came
  # through as its own AGE ("body=27 grip=252"), and the empty-HOME assertion above stayed green
  # the whole time. A gate must make the tool COMMIT to an answer only correct wiring can give.
  mkdir -p "$_ocs/.mesh"
  printf '42264|STILL|1||219834|0\n' > "$_ocs/.mesh/.body-motion-state"
  printf 'HELD 5 17593\n'            > "$_ocs/.mesh/.grip-state"
  printf 'LOUD\n'                    > "$_ocs/.mesh/.ambient-level"
  printf 'DARK|dwell_s=138|changes_24h=29\n' > "$_ocs/.mesh/.light-state"
  printf 'HERE 28:11:A5:B8:9E:A2 LE-Bose Revolve SoundLink\n' > "$_ocs/.mesh/.proximity.state"
  _e="$(HOME="$_ocs" bash "$0" --verbose 2>&1)"
  case "$_e" in *AT_COMPUTER*) : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: fresh real-format fixtures must classify AT_COMPUTER end-to-end (got '$_e')"; _f=1 ;; esac
  case "$_e" in *"body=STILL"*) : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: the live reader did not deliver the body VALUE (got '$_e')"; _f=1 ;; esac
  case "$_e" in *"grip=HELD"*)  : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: the live reader did not deliver the grip VALUE (got '$_e')"; _f=1 ;; esac
  case "$_e" in *"light=DARK"*) : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: the live reader did not deliver the light VALUE (got '$_e')"; _f=1 ;; esac
  case "$_e" in *"prox=HERE"*)  : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: the live reader did not deliver the prox VALUE (got '$_e')"; _f=1 ;; esac
  # ...and the same fixtures aged past the lease must flip it back to blind, through the same path
  find "$_ocs/.mesh" -type f -exec touch -d '3 hours ago' {} +
  _e2="$(HOME="$_ocs" bash "$0" 2>&1)"
  case "$_e2" in *UNCERTAIN*) : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: fixtures aged past the lease must go UNCERTAIN end-to-end (got '$_e2')"; _f=1 ;; esac
  case "$_e2" in *"body:stale"*) : ;; *) echo "  FAIL: the aged reading must be named STALE, not blind (got '$_e2')"; _f=1 ;; esac
  rm -rf "$_ocs"

  [ "$_f" = 0 ] && { echo "smoke-test: ok (6 classifications on REAL producer formats + fault-1 sentinel asserts [the live 19:28Z OFFLINE/OFFLINE reading is UNCERTAIN not RESTING, both organs named, 8 sentinel spellings, empty string] + fault-2 lease asserts [stale/fresh both directions, lease exceeds the 600s cadence, missing file = blind] + fault-3 prox asserts [missing and stale prox do NOT gate, blindness still shown, verdict identical across HERE vs OUT_OF_RANGE] + fault-4 parser asserts [pipe-annotated LIT reads BRIGHT, bare shape, annotated DARK, legacy bracketed body tag, light OFFLINE+ts] + read_input asserted through the live DESTRUCTURING [value, 2h age, absent = age -1 AND empty value, and a missing input reaching the classifier as blindness not as the literal -1] + output-switch asserts [--verbose/--json/default each reach their OWN branch, an empty HOME reads UNCERTAIN])"; exit 0; }
  echo "smoke-test: FAIL"; exit 1
fi

# `--verbose` set a VERBOSE flag nobody read while the output switch keyed on $MODE, so the
# documented `--verbose` silently produced the plain one-line form. A flag that parses and does
# nothing is worse than an unknown one: an unknown flag can at least be refused.
MODE=text; EDGE=0
for a in "$@"; do case "$a" in --json) MODE=json;; --edge) EDGE=1;; --verbose) MODE=verbose;; esac; done

TS=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)

# --- Read inputs (value + age; the age is half the claim) ------------------------------------
IFS=$'\t' read -r _body_age  _body_raw  <<<"$(read_input "$HOME/.mesh/.body-motion-state")"
IFS=$'\t' read -r _grip_age  _grip_raw  <<<"$(read_input "$HOME/.mesh/.grip-state")"
IFS=$'\t' read -r _amb_age   _amb_raw   <<<"$(read_input "$HOME/.mesh/.ambient-level")"
IFS=$'\t' read -r _light_age _light_raw <<<"$(read_input "$HOME/.mesh/.light-state")"
IFS=$'\t' read -r _prox_age  _prox_raw  <<<"$(read_input "$HOME/.mesh/.proximity.state")"

_rec="$(classify "$_body_raw" "$_body_age" "$_grip_raw" "$_grip_age" "$_amb_raw" "$_amb_age" \
                 "$_light_raw" "$_light_age" "$_prox_raw" "$_prox_age")"
tag="$(printf '%s' "$_rec" | cut -f1)"
state="$(printf '%s' "$_rec" | cut -f2)"
_body_motion="$(printf '%s' "$_rec" | cut -f3)"
_grip="$(printf '%s' "$_rec" | cut -f4)"
_ambient="$(printf '%s' "$_rec" | cut -f5)"
_light="$(printf '%s' "$_rec" | cut -f6)"
_prox="$(printf '%s' "$_rec" | cut -f7)"
[ -n "$state" ] || { echo "operator-context: n/a — classifier produced no record (python3 failed?)"; exit 2; }

# --- Read previous state ---
prev_state=""
if [ -f "$STATE" ]; then read -r prev_state _ < "$STATE" 2>/dev/null || true; fi

# --- Write state ---
printf '%s %s %s %s %s %s %s\n' "$state" "$_body_motion" "$_grip" "$_ambient" "$_light" "$_prox" "$TS" > "$STATE"

# --- Edge trigger ---
if [ "$EDGE" = 1 ]; then [ "$state" = "$prev_state" ] && exit 0; fi

# --- Output ---
case "$MODE" in
  json)
    printf '{"state":"%s","body":"%s","grip":"%s","ambient":"%s","light":"%s","prox":"%s","prox_gates":false,"lease_s":%s,"ts":"%s"}\n' \
      "$state" "$_body_motion" "$_grip" "$_ambient" "$_light" "$_prox" "$LEASE_S" "$TS"
    ;;
  verbose)
    printf '%s %s — body=%s grip=%s ambient=%s light=%s prox=%s (reported, not fused) lease=%ss\n' \
      "$tag" "$state" "$_body_motion" "$_grip" "$_ambient" "$_light" "$_prox" "$LEASE_S"
    ;;
  *)
    printf '%s %s\n' "$tag" "$state"
    ;;
esac
